   139	
   140	## Units of analysis and intervals
   141	
   142	- D1/D3: the star is the unit. Wilson 95% on unweighted proportions; plain
   143	  Wilson on the negatives class (weights cancel); survey bootstrap for PPV;
   144	  ESS-Wilson only for other descriptive weighted proportions, labeled
   145	  approximate.
   146	- D2: the TESS target (TIC) is the CLUSTER; inference is CONDITIONAL on the
   147	  frozen window assignment (report unique window count and reuse table —
   148	  windows repeat across targets, and a target-only bootstrap does not
   149	  represent the 928-window frame; stated as a limitation).
   150	  Estimator: per-target mean over its replicates within a scenario/stratum;
   151	  aggregate = equal-weight mean over the 103 targets (a scenario mix, NOT
   152	  the 928-window frame). Bootstrap: resample the 103 TICs with replacement
   153	  (B = 2000, frozen seed 20260830), carrying ALL of a resampled target's
   154	  replicates, paired census/L-S outcomes, phases, and scenario results
   155	  jointly; identical resample draws across scenarios (common random
   156	  numbers). Percentile 95% intervals; if a statistic is degenerate
   157	  (all-0/all-1), report the exact one-sided CP bound at the target level
   158	  instead. Pooled exact McNemar is PROHIBITED for D2; use the target-cluster
   159	  paired-difference bootstrap.
   160	- Sensitivity contrasts (D2 ladder, phase draws, amplitude-stationarity,
   161	  dominant-mode dropout — ALL core and binding; the ±30% multiplier is a
   162	  local sensitivity, never presented as an astrophysical uncertainty
   163	  envelope):
   164	  COMMON-SUBSET RULE — every contrast against nominal is computed with
   165	  nominal re-evaluated on the same median-window (K=1) subset and the same
   166	  bootstrap draws. Min-max across the 3x3 grid is a "prespecified
   167	  finite-grid sensitivity range", never a confidence band; endpoint
   168	  scenarios identified. De-dilution and amplitude-stationarity are separate
   169	  axes.
